This the source to the O88 optimizer.

It seems to be a copy of it's "development" directory, and as
such has some cruft in it, and the source itself is in a state
of flux (seems to have some debugging printf() statments, though
the code works).

Some of the files were "broken", and have been fixed.  The original
files are in the BADFILES directory, in case you're interested.
The "broken" files are:
   O88.EXE  -- This version did not work.  It was replaced with O88
               from the RELEASED directory.
   MAKEFILE -- Very nice, but the author forgot the DATA.C file
   FILES    -- The author forgot to link in OBJ\DATA

While the documentation says that O88 works with the 3.03 compiler,
the MAKEFILE (fixed) uses the -px (#pragma extensions) directive,
which seems to imply that the author was playing with compiling
the optimizer with/for the 3.1h compiler.

The CC program only wants to be compiled with the 3.03 compiler,
though O88 itself can be complied with either the 3.03 or 3.1h
compiler.  "Make" files for both compilers (303_O88.BAT and
31H_O88.BAT) are included.  For either compiler, copy the compiler
itself (C88.EXE, GEN.EXE, ASM88.EXE, BIND.EXE, *.H, CSTDIO.S) into
the current diretory.

The O88 optimizer must be used to compile the O88 optimizer,
otherwise the program overflows the 64K available to a small memory
model program.
